## DESCRIPTION
##   Identify Perpendicular Vectors
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## Tagged by nhamblet

## DBsubject(Geometry)
## DBchapter(Vector geometry)
## DBsection(Dot product, length, and unit vectors)
## Date(8/23/07)
## Institution(Union College)
## MLT(VectorsParallelOrthogNeither)
## Level(3)
## TitleText1('Calculus: Early Transcendentals')
## AuthorText1('Rogawski')
## EditionText1('1')
## Section1('12.3')
## Problem1('13')
## KEYWORDS('Vector', 'Perpendicular', 'Dot Product')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserPopUp.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Vector");

@u = ($a, $b, $c) = (
    2 * non_zero_random(-3, 3),
    2 * non_zero_random(-3, 3),
    non_zero_random(-5, 5)
);

$U = Vector(@u);
$V = Vector(random(-5, 5),          non_zero_random(-5, 5), random(-5, 5));
$W = Vector(non_zero_random(-5, 5), non_zero_random(-5, 5), random(-5, 5));

@vectors = (
    Vector($b / 2,  -$a / 2,     0),
    Vector($b - $c, 6 * $c - $a, $a - 6 * $b),
    $V, $W
);

@dd = map {
    DropDown([ 'perpendicular', 'not perpendicular' ], $_ . $U == 0 ? 0 : 1)
} @vectors;

@shuffle = random_subset(4, 0 .. 3);

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

BEGIN_PGML

Suppose [`\vec{u} = [$U]`].  Determine if each vector below is perpendicular to [`\vec{u}`]. 

a) [`` [$vectors[$shuffle[0]]] ``] [_]{$dd[$shuffle[0]]}

b) [`` [$vectors[$shuffle[1]]] ``] [_]{$dd[$shuffle[1]]}

c) [`` [$vectors[$shuffle[2]]] ``] [_]{$dd[$shuffle[2]]}

d) [`` [$vectors[$shuffle[3]]] ``] [_]{$dd[$shuffle[3]]}

END_PGML

@dots =  map { $_ . $U } @vectors[@shuffle];

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
For each, check the dot product with [` \vec{u}`].  If the result is 0, then 
the two vector are perpendicular. 

a) [`` [$vectors[$shuffle[0]]] \cdot [$U] = [$dots[0]] ``].  Therefore the two vectors are [$dd[$shuffle[0]]].

b) [`` [$vectors[$shuffle[1]]] \cdot [$U] = [$dots[1]] ``].  Therefore the two vectors are [$dd[$shuffle[1]]].

c) [`` [$vectors[$shuffle[2]]] \cdot [$U] = [$dots[2]] ``].  Therefore the two vectors are [$dd[$shuffle[2]]].

d) [`` [$vectors[$shuffle[3]]] \cdot [$U] = [$dots[3]] ``].  Therefore the two vectors are [$dd[$shuffle[2]]].


END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
